<article class="env-definition" id="02VC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02VC">Definition <span data-tag="02VC">39.18.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid scheme over $S$. Let $g : U' \to U$ be a morphism of schemes. The morphism of groupoids $(U', R', s', t', c') \to (U, R, s, t, c)$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/02VB" data-tag="02VB">39.18.1</a> is called the <em>restriction of $(U, R, s, t, c)$ to $U'$</em>. We sometime use the notation $R' = R|_{U'}$ in this case. </p>
</article>